## 🐛 Bugs Fixed

| # | File | Bug | Fix |
|---|------|-----|-----|
| 1 | `backend/app/services/post_service.py` | Post images were saved to `tempfile.gettempdir()` (OS temp dir, wiped on reboot) and stored as absolute filesystem paths — making them inaccessible via URL | Changed save directory to the persistent `backend/uploads/` folder served by FastAPI `StaticFiles`; return `/uploads/<filename>` URL path instead of absolute path |
| 2 | `backend/app/services/auth_service.py` | `name` field was not included in the JWT token payload or the login/signup response — users always appeared nameless after login | Added `name` to both the JWT payload and the `AuthResponse` return dict in `signup_user()` and `login_user()` |
| 3 | `backend/app/models/user.py` | `AuthResponse` Pydantic model was missing the `name` field — backend would silently drop it even if the service returned it | Added `name: str = ""` to `AuthResponse` |
| 4 | `frontend/lib/api.ts` — `login()` | User `name` was derived from `email.split("@")[0]` instead of the actual name stored in the database | Updated to use `raw.name` from the backend response (with email fallback) |
| 5 | `frontend/lib/api.ts` — `createPost()` | Return type was typed as `{ message: string; post_id: string }` but the backend actually returns a full `PostResponse` object | Fixed return type to `PostResponse` |
| 6 | `frontend/lib/api.ts` — `getPosts()` | Image paths (`/uploads/...`) were used as-is, causing broken images since they are relative paths that need the API base URL | Prepend `API_BASE_URL` to relative image paths so `<img src>` resolves correctly |
| 7 | `frontend/components/post-card.tsx` | `likes` state was initialized with `Math.random()` causing a React SSR/client hydration mismatch | Replaced with a stable seed derived from `post.id` set inside `useEffect` (client-only) |
| 8 | `frontend/components/image-upload.tsx` | Preview image was not cleared when the parent component reset the `value` prop to `null` (e.g. after form submit), leaving a stale preview visible | Added a `useEffect` that watches the `value` prop and clears `preview` state when `value` becomes falsy |

